---
import Layout from "../layouts/Practice.astro";
import { LINKS } from "../config/links";
const updated = "November 1, 2026";
---
<Layout title="Terms of use · The Practice" description="The terms for this site, in plain words. These terms cover innerboardsuite.com. Practice by InnerBoard, the app, has its own terms inside the app." path="/terms">
  <section class="view">
    <div class="phero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow ruled">Terms of use</p>
        <h1 style="margin-top:18px;max-width:18ch">The terms for this site, in plain words.</h1>
        <p class="lede" style="margin-top:22px">Last updated {updated}. These terms cover innerboardsuite.com. Practice by InnerBoard, the app, has its own terms inside the app.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="band">
      <div class="wrap legal">
    <h2>Using the site</h2>
    <p>You may read, link to and share the pages on this site. You may not copy the frameworks, curriculum descriptions, lesson content or course descriptions for commercial use without written permission from InnerBoard.</p>
    <h2>What the content is</h2>
    <p>Everything here describes an approach to self-leadership, coaching and organizational development. It is educational. It is not medical, psychological, legal or financial advice, and reading it does not create a client relationship with InnerBoard.</p>
    <h2>The Practice Coach and the Company OS Score</h2>
    <p>The Practice Coach and the Company OS Score are reflection and development tools, not clinical or professional assessments. What they show is produced from your own answers. Decisions you make from them are yours.</p>
    <h2>INQ Certification</h2>
    <p>Enrollment in INQ Certification is a separate agreement, made at the time of enrollment, with its own terms covering payment, access and the license to teach and coach from the frameworks.</p>
    <h2>Links to other places</h2>
    <p>Buttons on this site open Practice by InnerBoard, which has its own terms.</p>
    <h2>Ownership</h2>
    <p>InnerBoard, Practice by InnerBoard, InnerBoard Academy, InnerLab, INQ, InnerBoard IOS, the InnerBoard mark and the names of the frameworks are the property of InnerBoard.</p>
    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>The site is provided as it is. To the extent the law allows, InnerBoard is not liable for loss arising from your use of the site or your reliance on its content.</p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${LINKS.contactEmail}`}>{LINKS.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
        <p class="small">Written in plain language; to be reviewed by counsel before launch.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

